apt 2.7.14 cmake: fix GNUInstallDirs LIBEXECDIR on OHOS (bin -> lib)

apt's CMake works around a GNUInstallDirs bug by pinning
CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBEXECDIR to "lib", but only when /etc/debian_version
exists.  On OHOS/musl that file is absent, and CMake does not know the
HarmonyOS platform, so GNUInstallDirs resolves LIBEXECDIR to "bin".
The libexec helpers (apt-helper, solvers, planners, methods) then try to
install into <prefix>/bin/apt/... while the `apt` binary already exists
at <prefix>/bin/apt, and `make install` fails with:

  CMake Error at cmdline/cmake_install.cmake:121 (file):
    file INSTALL destination:
    /storage/Users/currentUser/test-install-apt-pkg-2.7.14/usr/local/bin/apt
    is not a directory.

Verified: /etc/debian_version does not exist on the OHOS host; config.h
had `#define LIBEXEC_DIR "/usr/local/bin/apt"`.

Fix: extend the existing workaround to also pin LIBEXECDIR to "lib" when
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is HarmonyOS, restoring the Debian layout
(<prefix>/lib/apt for libexec tools, <prefix>/bin for the apt CLI).
Inert on Debian.
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -28,7 +28,12 @@
 set(CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS_COVERAGE "-lgcov")
 
 # Work around bug in GNUInstallDirs
-if (EXISTS "/etc/debian_version")
+# Debian 上 /etc/debian_version 存在 -> libexec 放 <prefix>/lib/apt；
+# OHOS/musl 没有该文件，而 CMake 不认识 HarmonyOS 平台，GNUInstallDirs 会把
+# LIBEXECDIR 解析成 bin，导致 apt-helper 等 libexec 工具与 apt 本体二进制都
+# 装进 <prefix>/bin，cmake install 直接失败（destination /usr/local/bin/apt
+# is not a directory）。这里对 OHOS 同样固定为 "lib"，保持 Debian 布局。
+if (EXISTS "/etc/debian_version" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "HarmonyOS")
   set(CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBEXECDIR "lib")
 endif()
 

